## The VM for many sockets on one CPU (the race's box: 1 CPU, 1 GB).

## Processes (one per socket) and ports (sockets), sized to the box: a GB
## holds tens of thousands of sockets, not millions, and both tables are
## allocated whole at boot (the defaults, 1,048,576 processes and 65,536
## ports, are too big and too small).
+P 262144
+Q 262144
## One scheduler, for one CPU.
+S 1:1
## No busy-waiting when idle: spinning schedulers burn the CPU quota.
+sbwt none
+sbwtdcpu none
+sbwtdio none
